I would be careful of including too much more information than is 
included in the Guidebook presently, partly because it shouldn't be too 
spoily, and partly because it's already long and complicated enough that 
many players simply don't bother with it.

What I would like to see is, for the most part, the same information 
reorganized in such a manner that it is more readable: i.e., basic game 
information and strategy tips up front, tables of items, ascii symbols, 
etc. in the back (perhaps in appendices). Simply putting the thing into 
ordinary text--without hyphenation, spacing to create justified margins, 
and the silly headers and footers that make no sense unless you're 
printing it out--would be an immense benefit.

You may also want to simply Google for "Guidebook" to see what I and 
others have suggested in the past.

